    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0458" n="1292" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/674</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-26T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2440. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1502. Embassy’s 3001, October 22, 6 p.m., your 1723. We concur in the opinion
                    expressed by you in your letter of September 19, No. 5418,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d374-f1"/> that the total purchase should be considered as a whole
                    and any part taken by any of the Governments or sold be considered <pb
                        facs="0459" n="1293" xml:id="pg1293"/> for the trio account. In other words,
                    the proceeds of all resales should be pooled and divided equally among the three
                    Associated countries. We assume the resale prices will be submitted for approval
                    to the three Governments. We are now preparing a plan for handling the resales
                    and will submit it to you shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
